  "notes": "Patan Durbar Square, Mangal Bazar, Kumaripati and the Lagankhel edge: dense four-storey Newari brick lanes around the royal square. The Durbar Square temples, the Taleju temple, the Taleju bell house and the bahals get temple brick with pitched roofs and their real storey counts in place of the one-metre height tags; the palace blocks and the Kumari house keep brick with flat roofs; the hospital, the mall, the schools, the bank and shop buildings in the south become flat-roofed institutional or RCC; nine footprints under 5 m2 around the square are removed."
